# Escape hatch:
#   git push --no-verify

# tsc is the ONLY thing that checks types here — vitest strips them.
pnpm run typecheck || exit 1

# Byte-compares the generated capability declarations against what the Zod
# schemas render. Seconds, and it catches a drift class that CI would otherwise
# report minutes later.
pnpm run capabilities:dts:check || exit 1

# NOTE ON WHAT IS *NOT* IN pre-push.
#
# The worker suite is deliberately absent. It has been measured on this machine
# at 205-492 seconds — 75 files, 1078 tests in workerd against real D1, queues
# and Durable Objects, plus a dashboard build on a cold turbo cache. A hook that
# costs five minutes is a hook people learn to pass --no-verify to, which would
# cost the two fast checks above as well.
#
# typecheck and capabilities:dts:check are the high-yield half: together they
# run in seconds and catch the failures most likely to reach a push. The suite
# runs in CI on every push and pull request, which is where a five-minute job
# belongs.
